## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

### Changes Made:

#### 1. Package Installation
- **Added dependency**: `@vercel/analytics` (version 2.0.1)
- **Modified files**:
  - `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics to dependencies
  - `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies (368 packages added)

#### 2. Analytics Configuration
- **Modified file**: `app/layout.tsx`
- **Changes**:
  - Imported the Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag of the RootLayout

### Implementation Details:

This project uses **Next.js with the App Router**, so I followed the framework-specific instructions from the official Vercel documentation:

1. Installed the `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
2. Imported `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/next` in the root layout
3. Added the `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body element

The Analytics component is now properly configured to track page views and web vitals when deployed to Vercel.

### Testing:

- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ No TypeScript errors
- ✅ Static and dynamic routes generated correctly
- ✅ All dependencies installed successfully

### Next Steps:

Once deployed to Vercel, the analytics will automatically start tracking:
- Page views
- Web Vitals (FCP, LCP, CLS, FID, TTFB)
- Custom events (if configured)

Users can view analytics data in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab for this project.

### Files Modified:
- `front/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component
- `front/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `front/package-lock.json` - Updated lockfile with new dependencies
